  "finding": "The nav organises by SIX different axes at once — capability, vertical, job-to-be-done, role, integration platform, and implementation surface. That is not disorganisation; it is six legitimate entry models competing for one horizontal bar. It is also the strongest structural argument for search-led navigation, because a search box can serve all six axes simultaneously where a menu must pick an order."
